<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communist Party of the Soviet Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CPSU, Bolshevik Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Communist Party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> grew out of Lenin's Bolshevik faction and took power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> of 1917. It was the only legal party of the Soviet Union, governing through soviets and the secret police, with branches led by first secretaries in each Soviet republic. It lost its monopoly of power in 1990 and was banned after the failed coup of August 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union.jpg" alt="Communist Party of the Soviet Union" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kosogorsky Yaroslav, and others. · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D0%9F%D0%A1%D0%A1.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the <b>Bolsheviks</b> seized power the Maapäev declared itself the supreme authority in November 1917 and set up a Salvation Committee of Konstantin Päts, Jüri Vilms and Konstantin Konik.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Republic of Estonia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Real power lay with the <b>Communist Party of the Soviet Union</b>, whose Politburo and General Secretary directed state, economy and society; the party's leading role was written into the 1977 constitution.</blockquote><a href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>After the 20th Congress of the <b>Communist Party of the Soviet Union</b> in February 1956, with a more critical view of Stalin's rule, the text was altered.</blockquote><a href="/songs/lied-der-partei">Lied der Partei</a></li><li><blockquote>Its music was composed by Alexander Alexandrov in 1938 as the Hymn of the <b>Bolshevik Party</b>; its opening bars came from an earlier piece of his, &quot;Life Has Become Better&quot;, based on words Joseph Stalin had spoken at the First All-Union Meeting of the Stakhanovites on 17 November…</blockquote><a href="/songs/state-anthem-of-the-soviet-union">State Anthem of the Soviet Union</a></li><li><blockquote>In April 1920 the Red Army invaded, and the government ceded power to the <b>Bolsheviks</b>, creating the Azerbaijan SSR.</blockquote><a href="/state/azerbaijan-democratic-republic">Azerbaijan Democratic Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>Heydar Aliyev led the republic's <b>Communist Party</b> from 1969 to 1982.</blockquote><a href="/state/azerbaijan-ssr">Azerbaijan SSR</a></li></ul></section>
